post_install() {
    cat <<'MSG'

  Nx Witness Client (Open Source) installed.

    Launch : nxwitness-client   (or "Nx Witness Client (Open Source)" in the menu)
    Connect: https://<server-ip>:7001

  The launcher creates ~/.config/nx_ini/desktop_client.ini with demoMode=1 on first
  run for each user. That setting is REQUIRED: an Nx Witness server reports its
  customization as "default" while this build is branded metavms, and without it the
  client refuses to connect.

  The UI is branded "Nx Meta" - the same product, developer-edition branding.
  A "Beta version" dialog appears on every launch; it is harmless. Decline any client
  update offer: an official package would not run on Arch.

MSG
}

post_upgrade() {
    post_install
}

post_remove() {
    cat <<'MSG'

  Per-user settings were left in place. To remove them:
      rm -rf ~/.config/nx_ini/desktop_client.ini
      rm -rf ~/.local/share/"Network Optix" ~/.config/"Network Optix"

MSG
}
